{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q15628166","formula":"FeSi","hill":"FeSi","elements":["Si","Fe"],"composition":{"Fe":1.0,"Si":1.0},"names":{"en":"Iron silicide","ru":"Силицид железа"},"descriptions":{"en":"Iron monosilicide (FeSi) is an intermetallic compound, a silicide of iron that occurs in nature as the rare mineral naquite. It is a narrow-bandgap semiconductor with a room-temperature electrical resistivity of around 10 kΩ·cm and unusual magnetic properties at low temperatures. FeSi has a cubic crystal lattice with no inversion center; therefore its magnetic structure is helical, with right-hand and left-handed chiralities.","ru":"Силицид железа — бинарное неорганическое соединение железа и кремния с формулой FeSi, желтовато-серые кристаллы, не растворяется в воде."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":13956050,"mass":83.93,"charge":0,"smiles":"[Si].[Fe]","inchikey":"XWHPIFXRKKHEKR-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"iron;silicon","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-871","atoms":8,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[4.402,0.0,0.0],[0.0,4.402,0.0],[0.0,0.0,4.402]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":3.799,"y":2.804,"z":1.598,"el":"Fe"},{"x":2.804,"y":1.598,"z":3.799,"el":"Fe"},{"x":1.598,"y":3.799,"z":2.804,"el":"Fe"},{"x":0.603,"y":0.603,"z":0.603,"el":"Fe"},{"x":0.699,"y":1.502,"z":2.9,"el":"Si"},{"x":1.502,"y":2.9,"z":0.699,"el":"Si"},{"x":2.9,"y":0.699,"z":1.502,"el":"Si"},{"x":3.704,"y":3.704,"z":3.704,"el":"Si"}],"bonds":[[0,6,1],[0,7,1],[1,4,1],[1,7,1],[2,7,1],[2,5,1],[0,5,1],[1,6,1],[2,4,1],[3,4,1],[3,5,1],[3,6,1]],"cellOrigin":[0,0,0]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q15628166","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_monosilicide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"desc